# The web application is built, tested and released independently of the
# gateway binary, so it owns its ignores rather than relying on entries in the
# repository root. Everything listed here is regenerated by `npm ci`,
# `npm run build`, or a test run.

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/

# Test artifacts
#
# The Playwright config writes its output to a temporary directory, so these do
# not normally appear. They are listed because they are what Playwright writes
# by default, and neither a config change nor a direct --output invocation
# should be able to put screenshots and traces into a commit.
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Visual baselines.
#
# The browser suite is a local tool and no longer runs in CI, so a baseline is
# whatever the developer's own machine rendered — a committed one would only
# report that their fonts differ from the author's. Note the cost: Playwright
# writes a missing baseline and fails that first run, so a second run compares
# against the image it just produced. Style drift is caught only within a
# session that already had a baseline, not across a fresh clone.
e2e/*-snapshots/

# TypeScript incremental build state
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment overrides.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed value into the published bundle, so a file
# left here would ship its contents to every browser that loads the dashboard.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and operating system noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
